Fix reading compressed inline extents

read_compressed_inline() passes the extent *type* (BTRFS_FILE_EXTENT_INLINE,
0) to btrfs_decompress() instead of the extent's compression algorithm, so
every compressed inline file fails with "invalid compression algorithm: 0".
Hits any small file (< sectorsize) on a filesystem written with compress=.

Present in upstream btrfs-fuse as of b03483b. Drop this patch once upstream
fixes it.

--- a/data.c
+++ b/data.c
@@ -327,7 +327,7 @@
 	u32 csize = btrfs_file_extent_inline_item_len(path->nodes[0],
 						btrfs_item_nr(path->slots[0]));
 	u32 dsize = btrfs_file_extent_ram_bytes(path->nodes[0], fi);
-	u8 compression = btrfs_file_extent_type(path->nodes[0], fi);
+	u8 compression = btrfs_file_extent_compression(path->nodes[0], fi);
 	char *cbuf;
 	int ret;
 
